# Plan management rules - PRIORITY

`plan/PLAN.md` is the single source of truth for execution. Read
`.agents/skills/plan-keeper/SKILL.md` for the full workflow and
`.agents/rules/product-discipline.mdc` for the mandatory product-scope gate.

## Before starting work
- **Read `plan/PLAN.md`.** Understand the current phase and the build order
  (timeline + patch engine → render + validation → AI → compositing → agent mode).
- Find the task you are about to do. If it isn't there, **add it** as `[ ]` in the right phase.
- For non-trivial feature or architecture work, record the scope gate before expanding the plan:
  - concrete user outcome;
  - current workflow gap;
  - minimum end-to-end vertical slice;
  - existing systems to reuse;
  - intentionally deferred adjacent scope;
  - evidence required for completion.
- If the task introduces a subsystem, editing domain, runtime/provider/worker boundary, a large
  sub-plan, multiple ADRs, or broad cross-layer work, run a product-scope review before treating
  the expansion as approved scope.

## While working
- Mark the task **`[~]` (in progress)** when you start.
- **Add new tasks** you discover (`[ ]`). Mark blocked work `[!]` with a one-line reason.
- Do not automatically promote every discovered adjacent opportunity into active scope. Record it
  as deferred unless it is required for the current vertical slice or explicitly chosen by the
  maintainer.
- If a sub-area genuinely needs its own plan, create a new doc under `plan/` and link it from
  `PLAN.md`. The sub-plan must identify the near-term executable vertical slice it enables.
- Keep plan detail proportional to uncertainty and risk. A long document is not evidence of
  implementation progress.

## When done
- Mark **`[x]`** ONLY when the Definition of Done is met and the applicable verification passed.
  **Never check off untested or unverified work.**
- A schema, worker, backend, tool, placeholder UI, hardcoded demo path, ADR, or plan does not by
  itself justify `[x]` for an editing capability.
- For an editing capability, confirm the applicable path is usable end to end: user entry → target
  resolution → operation/tool → validation → preview → render/export semantics → undo → failure
  state → tests.
- Keep the **"Status snapshot"** line and the **"Last updated"** date current.

## Reconcile
- Keep the plan honest: if code state and plan disagree, fix the plan to match reality and note it.
- If a capability was previously marked complete but its actual UI/preview/render/AI path is not
  usable, reopen it instead of preserving an inaccurate completion claim.
- Preserve explicit maintainer scope decisions and their rationale so later agents do not
  repeatedly reopen settled product choices.

The legend is `[ ]` not started · `[~]` in progress · `[x]` done · `[!]` blocked.
